; frame.tal - a border four pixels thick.
;
;   ./duxasm -o roms/frame.rom asm/frame.tal
;   ./duxsdl roms/frame.rom
;
; The whole screen with a rectangle taken out of it: everything inside is left
; at the background, which is a cheaper way to describe a border than four edges
; that have to join up at the corners.
;
; Four tests, each of which jumps to the plot, and one fallthrough that skips.
; In that order. With the skip and the plot the other way round - which is how it
; was written first - the interior gets plotted too, and the result is a filled
; rectangle with a four pixel hole along one edge rather than a border.
;
; 320*200 - 312*192 = 64000 - 59904 = 4096 pixels.

INCLUDE "common.tal"

@draw
        JSR2 @clear
        LIT2 $0000
        STA2 $ZP.sj
@row
        LIT2 $0000
        STA2 $ZP.si
@col
        ; Inside x 4..315 and y 4..195 means not the border.
        LDA2 $ZP.si
        LIT2 $0004
        LTH2
        JNZ @border-top
        LDA2 $ZP.si
        LIT2 $013b
        GTH2
        JNZ @border-top
        LDA2 $ZP.sj
        LIT2 $0004
        LTH2
        JNZ @border-top
        LDA2 $ZP.sj
        LIT2 $00c3
        GTH2
        JNZ @border-top
        ; Not on the border, so nothing to draw. This is the *only* path that
        ; falls through, and having it draw is what put a filled rectangle
        ; inside the frame: the four tests above all jump to the plot, so a
        ; fallthrough that also plotted meant everything was plotted.
        JMP @col-end
@border-top
        LIT $01
        STA $ZP.t
        LDA2 $ZP.si
        STA2 $ZP.rx
        LDA2 $ZP.sj
        STA2 $ZP.ry
        LDZ2 $ZP.rx
        LDZ2 $ZP.ry
        LDZ $ZP.t
        JSR2 @plot
@col-end
        LDA2 $ZP.si
        LIT2 $0001
        ADD2
        STA2 $ZP.si
        LDA2 $ZP.si
        LIT2 $0140
        GTH2
        JNZ @col-end2
        JMP @col
@col-end2
        LDA2 $ZP.sj
        LIT2 $0001
        ADD2
        STA2 $ZP.sj
        LDA2 $ZP.sj
        LIT2 $00c8
        GTH2
        JNZ @row-end
        JMP @row
@row-end
        JMP2r2
